# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalvertex).
#
# Why these four, in this order: the generated vertex stage draws on the Adreno and its pixel
# matches, while Apple's own clearVertex dies in fd6_emit_3d_state with signal 11 (a null
# dereference at offset 0x208; the stack is in docs/metal.md 10.24). The one thing that
# distinguishes the two is that clearVertex writes NO varying at all -- it writes air.position
# and nothing else -- so the next question is whether a program with a varying survives.
#
# texturedVertex2D writes air.vertex_output `texcoord`, and texturedFragment2DUInt reads it;
# on softpipe that pair draws the interpolated picture (texel (0,0) at the near corner, texel
# (3,3) at the far one). If it draws here and clearVertex does not, the fault is about a
# program with no varyings, which is a narrow thing to go and look at.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw --vertex texturedVertex2D --fragment texturedFragment2DUInt /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw --vertex clearVertex /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
#
# And the same draw with the texture seeded one row at a time, which is how this test did it
# until now: four replaceRegion calls at a non-zero region origin. That is the second
# explanation of the flip in docs/metal.md 10.26 -- if those rows land in one place, every
# texel carries the last row's y = 203 and pixel (0, 0) reads 100 203 303 400 with no flip
# anywhere. The two lines differ in nothing else, so whichever way they disagree names the
# cause. The driver now also prints what it reads back out of the seeded texture, so the
# answer does not have to be inferred from the drawn pixel at all.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw --seed-rows --vertex texturedVertex2D --fragment texturedFragment2DUInt /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
